From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fanasina RANDRIATSARAFARA <m.randriatsarafara.f@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 11:15:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8475-xiaomi-diting: Keep L7C and L11C
 on for the fingerprint sensor

The Goodix under-display fingerprint sensor is driven by the secure
world over an SPI bus Linux does not see, so no Linux driver ever
votes for its supplies. Confirmed this session, empirically, by
forcing them on from a test kernel module: the sensor is supplied by
L7C (vreg_l7c_3p0) and L11C (vreg_l11c_2p5) on this board revision, not
L1C/L3C as an earlier version of this patch assumed from the vendor
devicetree's generic "fingerprint_goodix" label without checking which
LDOs it actually resolved to on this specific unit. Keep both on.

The sensor reset (TLMM 41) is left to user space, which has to pulse it
the way the vendor HAL does.
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-diting.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-diting.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-diting.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-diting.dts
@@ -576,11 +576,20 @@
 			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
 		};
 
+		/*
+		 * Also the Goodix fingerprint sensor supply. The sensor is
+		 * driven by the secure world over its own SPI bus, so no
+		 * Linux driver claims it: keep it on, or the trusted
+		 * application cannot initialise the sensor (errors
+		 * 1043/1064).
+		 */
 		vreg_l7c_3p0: ldo7 {
 			regulator-name = "vreg_l7c_3p0";
 			regulator-min-microvolt = <3000000>;
 			regulator-max-microvolt = <3544000>;
 			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
+			regulator-boot-on;
+			regulator-always-on;
 		};
 
 		vreg_l8c_1p8: ldo8 {
@@ -604,11 +613,14 @@
 			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
 		};
 
+		/* Also the Goodix fingerprint sensor supply, see above. */
 		vreg_l11c_2p5: ldo11 {
 			regulator-name = "vreg_l11c_2p5";
 			regulator-min-microvolt = <2504000>;
 			regulator-max-microvolt = <3008000>;
 			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
+			regulator-boot-on;
+			regulator-always-on;
 		};
 
 		vreg_l12c_1p8: ldo12 {
